  "replication_unit": "calibration EVENT. Rows within an event are correlated, so neither N_cal*T nor N_cal*C is an independent sample count. All intervals here bootstrap the ten seed-level paired differences only.",
  "scale_dominance_note": "The per-axis sample estimators are unbiased only up to that same reciprocal scale: E[Sigma_c_hat] = Sigma_c * tr(Sigma_t)/T and E[Sigma_t_hat] = Sigma_t * tr(Sigma_c)/C. So kronecker_scale_ratio has an expected value of tr(Sigma_t)*tr(Sigma_c)/(C*T) rather than 1, and both kronecker_relative_frobenius_error and oracle_whitening_residual are dominated by that global factor rather than by estimation error. They are reported here exactly as the runbook defines them. The scale-free accuracy statements are the two shape errors. NFPA's fitted subspace and its reconstruction are invariant to a global rescaling of the whitening transform -- ALS minimises a scale-equivariant objective and the reconstruction unwhitens through the same scaled transform -- so this factor does not propagate into the reported held-out metrics.",
  "scope_note": "One fixed estimated-covariance condition: a measured sensitivity check, not a general covariance-robustness boundary.",
